From 10262ce4efdec5438a1b658e07f5ee857ef88bb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:04:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 322/395] Unified: the automatic dimensions of a drawing do not
 repeat or say nothing

On a connecting rod (engine field test 0.7.3) the centre distance came
twice (the overall size between the points, which the round ends pass),
a width of 23.64 was measured from the web's side to the hole, the hole
sizes' leaders ran across the part, and the thickness sat on the title
block. An overall size is given only when its points are the view's
extremes; hole positions are from a straight edge only when it is the
outermost, else from hole to hole; each hole size is beside its own hole;
a size that would fall on the title block goes above the view. Arcs that
go all round count as a hole's circle (a wall with seams).

Test: FreeCADCmd -t TestDrawingAuto

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
